## Hook Configuration Resolution

Updated `~/.claude/settings.json` to include ML hooks with project-specific matcher:

### Configuration Added

```json
{
    "hooks": {
        "SessionStart": [
            {
                "matcher": "cwd:Opus-code-test",
                "hooks": [
                    {
                        "type": "command",
                        "command": "bash /home/user/Opus-code-test/scripts/ml-session-start-hook.sh"
                    }
                ]
            }
        ],
        "PostToolUse": [
            {
                "matcher": "cwd:Opus-code-test",
                "hooks": [
                    {
                        "type": "command",
                        "command": "bash /home/user/Opus-code-test/scripts/ml-tool-capture-hook.sh"
                    }
                ]
            }
        ],
        "Stop": [
            {
                "matcher": "",
                "hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "~/.claude/stop-hook-git-check.sh"}]
            },
            {
                "matcher": "cwd:Opus-code-test",
                "hooks": [
                    {
                        "type": "command",
                        "command": "bash /home/user/Opus-code-test/scripts/ml-session-capture-hook.sh"
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    }
}
```

### Key Design Decisions

1. **Absolute paths**: Used `/home/user/Opus-code-test/scripts/` for reliability since global config
2. **cwd matcher**: `cwd:Opus-code-test` ensures hooks only run in this project
3. **Preserved git-check**: Existing global Stop hook kept with empty matcher (runs everywhere)
4. **Separate Stop entries**: ML Stop hook added as second entry, not merged with git-check
